Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:27:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] test(host-contracts): governance profile tests (timelock,
 guard, canary, pinning)

An OpenZeppelin TimelockController (7-day delay) owns the ACL and, through
ACLOwnable, the FHEVMExecutor. The upgrade guard still refuses a Core-less
implementation sent through the timelock. The operator canary (four views
on a retired account) catches a Core-less liar; a backdoored release that
spares the canary is caught only by implementation pinning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
